From: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Patch-mainline: never, kabi
References: bsc#1271050
Subject: [PATCH] kABI fix for KVM: x86/mmu: Track possible NX huge pages
 separately for TDP vs Shadow MMU (bsc#1271050)

Commit 6777885605e1 ("KVM: x86/mmu: Track possible NX huge pages separately
for TDP vs. Shadow MMU") replaces a list_head field in kvm_arch with a
kvm_possible_nx_huge_pages array. kvm_arch is only tracked as kABI-relevant
because some VFIO functions take a struct kvm pointer, which they pass back
to KVM internal functions and never access any fields. Thus, simply hide the
change from kABI checks.

Signed-off-by: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/kvm_host.h
@@ -1369,7 +1369,11 @@ struct kvm_arch {
 	bool pre_fault_allowed;
 	struct hlist_head mmu_page_hash[KVM_NUM_MMU_PAGES];
 	struct list_head active_mmu_pages;
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	struct kvm_possible_nx_huge_pages possible_nx_huge_pages[KVM_NR_MMU_TYPES];
+#else
+	struct list_head possible_nx_huge_pages;
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_KVM_EXTERNAL_WRITE_TRACKING
 	struct kvm_page_track_notifier_head track_notifier_head;
 #endif
